ule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jacob","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jacob::Jacob::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jacob"},"text":"Tremble, O earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob,","verse":7}],"id":"Jacob","label":"Jacob","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Jacob::Jacob::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Jacob","term":"Jacob"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Jacob","sourceTitle":"Jacob"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.1-117.2","r":"Ps.111.1-117.2","rawR":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.1-117.2","value":"Ps.111.1-117.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 111–117"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The refrain ",{"c":["Praise the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":["!"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (Hebrew ",{"c":["haleluyah"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") characterizes this group of psalms."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.111.1-117.2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":117,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":111,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.111.1-117.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[111,112,113,114,115,116,117],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"22b6425eac56925667128161925e7981d1b2aac4109f6fbee20150584747df92","sourceItemName":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7176,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.111.1-117.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.113.1-118.29","r":"Ps.113.1-118.29","rawR":"Ps.113.1-118.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.113.1-118.29","value":"Ps.113.1-118.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 113–118"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These psalms form what is known as the “Egyptian Hallel” (",{"c":["hallel"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," means “praise”) because Jews use the collection in the celebration of Passover, which was instituted at the beginning of the exodus from Egypt. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.113.1-114.8","r":"Ps.113.1-114.8","rawR":"Ps.113.1-114.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.113.1-114.8","value":"Ps.113.1-114.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalms 113–114"}," are recited before the Passover meal and ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.1-118.29","r":"Ps.115.1-118.29","rawR":"Ps.115.1-118.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.1-118.29","value":"Ps.115.1-118.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 115–118"}," afterward."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.113.1-118.29","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":118,"endVerse":29,"startChapter":113,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.113.1-118.29","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[113,114,115,116,117,118],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3bb66210be6b57d7effeab71c9a1a99f778790f8fc5109e3183b8ed871025210","sourceItemName":"Ps.113.1-118.29","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7191,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.113.1-118.29","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.113.1-118.29","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.1-8","r":"Ps.114.1-8","rawR":"Ps.114.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.1-8","value":"Ps.114.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 114"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This lyrical celebration of the Lord’s power in nature recalls Israel’s beginning as a nation at the Exodus (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.1-2","r":"Ps.114.1-2","rawR":"Ps.114.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.1-2","value":"Ps.114.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:1-2"},") and upon their entry to the Promised Land (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.3-6","r":"Ps.114.3-6","rawR":"Ps.114.3-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.3-6","value":"Ps.114.3-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:3-6"},"). It promotes reverence for the God of Jacob (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.7-8","r":"Ps.114.7-8","rawR":"Ps.114.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.7-8","value":"Ps.114.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:7-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.114.1-8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":114,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":114,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.114.1-8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[114],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0e0f3235a6490dad045d407b8103eaf87e9f107340d62bd18099fd10fb2fa89a","sourceItemName":"Ps.114.1-8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7199,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.114.1-8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.114.1-8","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.1-2","r":"Ps.114.1-2","rawR":"Ps.114.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.1-2","value":"Ps.114.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:1-2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," At the time of Israel’s exodus from Egypt and their entrance into the Promised Land, Israel was one holy ",{"c":["kingdom"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.19.5-6","r":"Exod.19.5-6","rawR":"Exod.19.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.19.5-6","value":"Exod.19.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 19:5-6"},"). • The separate references to ",{"c":["the land of Judah"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["Israel"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," indicate that the psalm was composed after the kingdom was divided (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.16-17","r":"1Kgs.12.16-17","rawR":"1Kgs.12.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.16-17","value":"1Kgs.12.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 12:16-17"},"; cp. ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.11.8","r":"1Sam.11.8","rawR":"1Sam.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.11.8","value":"1Sam.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sam 11:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.35","r":"1Kgs.1.35","rawR":"1Kgs.1.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.35","value":"1Kgs.1.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:35"},"), and probably after the Exile. The ",{"c":["land of Judah became God’s sanctuary"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," because the people worshiped God; his Tabernacle and later his Temple were located there."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.114.1-2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":114,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":114,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.114.1-2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[114],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ff5b2851e3231e12792e34015e22dc8a276aa6561ab42222917b260b60ddd77a","sourceItemName":"Ps.114.1-2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7200,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.114.1-2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.114.1-2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.3-4","r":"Ps.114.3-4","rawR":"Ps.114.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.3-4","value":"Ps.114.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:3-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["hurried out of their way!"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The waters divided for Israel to escape Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.77.17-18","r":"Ps.77.17-18","rawR":"Ps.77.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.77.17-18","value":"Ps.77.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"77:17-18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.14.1-31","r":"Exod.14.1-31","rawR":"Exod.14.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.14.1-31","value":"Exod.14.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 14"},"). • ",{"c":["The Jordan River turned away"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," when Israel arrived to cross over (see ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.3.1-17","r":"Josh.3.1-17","rawR":"Josh.3.1-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.3.1-17","value":"Josh.3.1-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Josh 3"},"). • ",{"c":["skipped like rams:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," God’s presence caused the mountains to quake (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.19.16-20","r":"Exod.19.16-20","rawR":"Exod.19.16-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.19.16-20","value":"Exod.19.16-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 19:16-20"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.114.3-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":114,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":114,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.114.3-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[114],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"98cf74238963b560986ae50f1c9d8f98355e5e2eb4ff6f3bedc77760c9b31168","sourceItemName":"Ps.114.3-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7201,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.114.3-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.114.3-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.114.8","r":"Ps.114.8","rawR":"Ps.114.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.114.8","value":"Ps.114.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"114:8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The Lord miraculously provided for his people in hard times after the Exile, just as he had done in the wilderness after the Exodus."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.114.8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":114,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":114,"startVerse":8}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.114.8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[114],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9932eecfb59e9ca34039124e9b2ca83b80e0e187af8324ce540fea065d86baa7","sourceItemName":"Ps.114.8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7202,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.114.8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.114.8","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}